WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.450
Picture a population
that doubles every hour:

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:09.210
1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32 thousand.

3
00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:12.110
Each hour adds more than the hour before.

4
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.950
The curve bends upward into a J.

5
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.370
Real yeast in a flask
starts out just like that.

6
00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:22.980
Then the curve bends over, and
the amount levels off near 660.

7
00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:28.440
So why does a population that doubles
again and again eventually stop growing?

8
00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:33.230
In this mission, you'll track the four
ways a population's numbers can change.

9
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:37.880
Then you'll see why a storm and a spreading
disease hit a crowded population in

10
00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:39.760
very different ways.

11
00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:44.660
Your mission: explain why a population
that doubles again and again eventually

12
00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:45.790
stops growing.
